# debug.keystore is deliberately COMMITTED (unusual, and on purpose):
# Colab regenerated a fresh keystore every build, which changed the app's
# SHA-1 fingerprint every time — making it impossible to ever register the
# app for Google sign-in. A debug keystore protects nothing (its passwords
# are the public Android defaults); a debug SHA-1 that never changes is
# worth far more than pretend-secrecy here. The RELEASE keystore, when
# created, must NEVER be committed.
